            <ArticleTitle>Cavernous hemangioma of tunica albuginea testis manifesting as testicular pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>673.e13-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cavernous hemangioma of the tunica albuginea of the testis is very rare; only 2 cases have been reported in published studies. Both cases presented as testicular masses. We report what we believe to be the third case of cavernous hemangioma of the tunica albuginea that manifested as pain without any mass.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
